bnk-forge is a deployment platform for F5 BIG-IP Next for Kubernetes: OpenTofu
pipelines, module catalogs, blueprints, fleets, RBAC and DPU provisioning.
bnkscope removed all of it and kept the one job that mattered during an
incident — look at the cluster and understand what is wrong. bnk-forge deploys
BNK; bnkscope looks at it.

The substantial majority of the code here originated in bnk-forge, and this
repository's git history begins with bnk-forge's own initial public release
commit, so the attribution is in the record and not only in this file.
docs/BNKSCOPE_PLAN.md documents the eight phases of the reduction, including
the parts of the plan that turned out to be wrong.

bnkscope is not maintained by the bnk-forge authors, and issues found here
should be reported here rather than to bnk-forge.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

bnkscope's TMM telemetry comes from tmmscope:

    https://github.com/mwiget/tmmscope
    Copyright 2026 Marcel Wiget
    Licensed under the MIT License

Two parts of it are vendored here rather than depended on:

  - `tmm-stat-exporter/` — the sidecar TMM Live injects, forked at `3948973`
    from tmmscope's `cmd/tmm-stat-exporter` and `internal/tmstat`. The MIT
    licence it carries is in `tmm-stat-exporter/LICENSE` and governs that
    directory; the rest of bnkscope is Apache-2.0.
  - `telemetry/` — the Prometheus and Grafana configuration and the two
    dashboards, copied from `internal/assets/files/` at the same commit.

bnkscope reimplemented the injection itself in Python (see ADR D-036); it needs
no tmmscope binary at runtime.
